+## What is implemented
+
+`study.py` provides the four required commands:
+
+```text
+python -m research.n1_v2.study validate-pack --manifest PATH
+python -m research.n1_v2.study intake --manifest PATH --captures PATH --output PATH
+python -m research.n1_v2.study run --intake PATH --receiver-config PATH --output PATH
+python -m research.n1_v2.study report --results PATH --output PATH
+```
+
+The controller now:
+
+- validates `nishan.n1-pack/v2`, unchanged carrier constants, split-specific matrices, canonical evaluator labels, every coupled SHA-256, the exhaustive artifact inventory and every declared non-escaping pack path;
+- inventories originals without copying or modifying them, including dimensions, byte hash, inode/device/mtime identity and read-only privacy-limited EXIF metadata;
+- keeps camera acquisition and transport as separate axes: a first-seen camera original arriving as a WhatsApp document remains an original-camera observation, while its byte-preservation status remains operator-declared/unverified without an independent matching sender hash;
+- distinguishes original camera files, separately linked byte-preserving WhatsApp retransfers, compressed WhatsApp photos, scanner continuous-tone, scanner bilevel, JPEG diagnostics and donor overlays;
+- resolves derivatives to an independent same-sheet original with the same phone/view, requires every fixed diagnostic parent to be the actual single-contributor phone-A/front original, and prevents identical bytes from becoming independent robustness cases;
+- prepares every receiver case without opening evaluator labels, writes and hashes a preparation commitment, rechecks the exact committed manifest and label bytes, then opens labels and scores;
+- validates the complete `prepared.json`/`evidence.npz`/`commitment.json` inventory, each stored array hash, scalar commitment, exact source/capture/config/prepared hashes, the eight-file receiver implementation mapping (including `watermark.py`), the canonical implementation hash, all 1,000 finite row scores, strict thresholds and profile-wide accusation unions;
+- uses the fixed decision budgets `108000`, `270000` and `1350000`, never shrinking after a failure;
+- retains preparation errors, registration failures, inconclusive profiles, scoring errors, abstentions, wrong-valid accusations and innocent accusations case by case;
+- reopens and hashes each scored row's materialized `prepared.json`/`commitment.json`, verifies its scalar commitment and eight-file implementation mapping, then revalidates the score against those exact code hashes before reporting paired global/local outcomes, detect-one success and all-member recall separately;
+- checks exact calibration sheet × view, validation artifact × phone × view and held-out artifact × phone × view cells rather than accepting balanced marginal totals;
+- drives advancement from the 48 c=5 cases, while reporting all 96 primary captures separately;
+- cluster-bootstraps the c=5 gain by page/artifact with seed `20260916` and 10,000 resamples;
+- derives projected page corners in original-capture pixels by inverting the accepted registration transform, retains the transform hash and corner measurement, and never substitutes whole-photo width for the >=1600-pixel page-width envelope;
+- refuses advancement with missing controls, unknown phone A/B, asymmetric or non-distinct identity evidence, incomplete printer settings, unmeasured/sub-1600 projected page width, incomplete full-page framing or view coverage;
+- requires one canonical Canon/paper/scale/driver/quality/colour settings signature across all 12 calibration captures, while requiring and reporting observed unprintable-margin clipping separately because it is an outcome rather than a controllable setting;
+- after the global preparation commitment and sole evaluator-label opening point, verifies the public synthetic codebook biases against committed receiver evidence and computes raw BER for the four marked originals from `hard_word` outside `hard_erased`;
+- refuses calibration completion without all four committed-array raw-BER records, both matched C1/C0 coupon pairs and their uncertainty-bearing regional records, or a stop unless 12 real physical calibration records have bound evidence and a predeclared rule cites all 12.
+
+`coupon_calibration.py` validates the nine-region exact-RGB-delta descriptor and performs source-only registration. It fits global gain/offset from multi-tone source/anchor pixels, then uses a rank-aware regional intercept plus centered delta-template fit. It reports clean endpoint energy separately from measured modulation, correlation, unexplained noise, clipping and a conditional residual-model interval. A near-zero well-conditioned gain is retained as negative evidence; a zero template, unidentifiable interval or rejected registration is inconclusive. Matching C0 controls are paired when present. These intervals explicitly exclude registration, spatial-correlation and print/camera systematics; neither they nor the conditional Wilson BER interval are physical-study confidence bounds. Coupons never enter Tardos attribution and never emit an automatic stop decision.
+
+## Frozen design and decision accounting
+
+The protocol was committed before orchestration tests in `b5513d0`, then clarified before the first green simulation in `9f95cb8` so the advancement denominator is the 48 c=5 cases rather than the easier all-96 aggregate.
+
+| Stage | Planned decisions | Physical photos | Primary denominator | H floor | Current state |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| Calibration | 12 | 12 | calibration only | 108,000 | 0/12, pending |
+| Validation | 30 | 20 | 16 | 270,000 | two local Task-4 contents and physical collection pending separately |
+| Held-out | 150 | 120 | 96 total / 48 c=5 endpoint | 1,350,000 | six local Task-4 contents and two-phone physical collection pending separately |
+
+The 150 held-out decisions are 96 primary captures, 24 unmarked physical controls and 30 derived diagnostics. The 120 physical files are the 96 primary plus 24 unmarked controls. Wrong-key, wrong-context, wrong-source, JPEG and donor-overlay diagnostics each require one case per held-out content and stay outside the primary denominator.
+
+Operational attribution uses each profile's sorted union across all frozen hypotheses. Evaluator attack labels only stratify reporting; they never choose the favorable score vector. A case with a contributor found under one hypothesis and an innocent accused under another is a failure with an innocent accusation.
